<title>ISRAEL: Israel's budget posts surplus in April.</title>
<headline>Israel's budget posts surplus in April.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel posted a total budget surplus of 341 million shekels in April, preliminary figures released by the Treasury on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>			 April 1997   March 1997     April 1996</p>
<p> Budget balance	+341	   +188		  + 391</p>
<p> Expenditures	 9,859	 13,784		  8,247</p>
<p> Receipts	    10,350	 14,110		  8,638</p>
<p>Note: Figures are in millions of shekels. April 1996 figures are in 1996 shekels.</p>
<p>The government had a deficit of 928 million shekels in the first four months of the year.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.41 shekels)</p>
</text>
